#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:3
msgid "学习任务的形式"
msgstr "Learning Task Formulations"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:5
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{doc}`computational-"
"graph`中介绍的计算图描述了数据如何在模型中流动。但数据流向什么样的目标？不同类型的\"规律\"需要不同的数学建模方式。"
msgstr ""
"The computational graph introduced in {doc}`computational-graph` describes how data flows through a model. But toward what objective does the data flow? Different types of \"patterns\" require different mathematical modeling approaches."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:7
msgid "机器学习在找什么规律？"
msgstr "What Patterns Does Machine Learning Look For?"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:9
#, python-brace-format
msgid "机器学习的本质是从数据中**发现规律**，然后用这些规律做预测 {cite}`bishop2006pattern`。但\"规律\"有不同形式："
msgstr "The essence of machine learning is to **discover patterns** from data and then use these patterns to make predictions {cite}`bishop2006pattern`. However, \"patterns\" come in different forms:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md
msgid "规律类型"
msgstr "Pattern Type"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md
msgid "核心问题"
msgstr "Core Question"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md
msgid "例子"
msgstr "Example"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md
msgid "**类别边界**"
msgstr "**Category Boundaries**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md
msgid "这类事物有什么共同特征？"
msgstr "What common features do things of this type share?"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md
msgid "识别猫和狗"
msgstr "Classifying cats and dogs"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md
msgid "**数值映射**"
msgstr "**Numerical Mappings**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md
msgid "输入输出是什么关系？"
msgstr "What is the relationship between input and output?"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md
msgid "根据面积预测房价"
msgstr "Predicting house prices based on area"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md
msgid "**序列依赖**"
msgstr "**Sequence Dependencies**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md
msgid "下一步应该是什么？"
msgstr "What should come next?"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md
msgid "续写句子"
msgstr "Completing a sentence"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:17
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"这三种规律对应三种任务类型：**分类**、**回归**和**自回归**。它们共享相同的{ref}`computational-"
"graph`计算机制，但目标的数学形式截然不同。"
msgstr ""
"These three pattern types correspond to three task formulations: **classification**, **regression**, and **autoregression**. They share the same computational mechanism in the {ref}`computational-graph`, but their target mathematical formulations are distinctly different."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:21
msgid "分类任务：发现类别边界的规律"
msgstr "Classification Tasks: Discovering Category Boundary Patterns"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:23
msgid "想象你在教小孩认动物。你不会给他看一张 checklist，而是指着图片说：\"这个有四条腿、有毛、会汪汪叫，所以是狗。\""
msgstr "Imagine teaching a child to recognize animals. Instead of showing them a checklist, you point at a picture and say, \"This one has four legs, fur, and barks, so it's a dog.\""

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:25
msgid "**分类的本质**：找到区分不同类别的**边界**——边界这边是A类，那边是B类。"
msgstr "**Essence of Classification**: Finding the **boundary** that separates different categories—class A on one side, class B on the other."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:27
msgid "在特征空间中，每个样本是一个点，分类就是画一条**决策边界**把空间切开："
msgstr "In feature space, each sample is a point, and classification is drawing a **decision boundary** that partitions the space:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:30
msgid "分类任务的决策边界"
msgstr "Decision Boundary in Classification Tasks"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:53
msgid "**关键洞察**："
msgstr "**Key Insights**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:55
msgid "边界这边聚集着同类样本"
msgstr "Samples of the same class cluster on one side of the boundary"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:56
msgid "边界是\"模糊\"的（软边界），不是一刀切的硬线"
msgstr "Boundaries are \"soft\" (probabilistic) rather than rigid hard cuts"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:57
msgid "新样本落在哪边，就预测为哪类"
msgstr "A new sample is predicted as whichever class its location falls into"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:59
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**数学形式**：分类模型输出类别概率分布 $p(y=k|x)$，其中 $k \\in \\{1, 2, ..., "
"K\\}$。决策规则是选择概率最大的类别："
msgstr ""
"**Mathematical Formulation**: A classification model outputs a class probability distribution $p(y=k|x)$, where $k \\in \\{1, 2, ..., K\\}$. The decision rule selects the class with maximum probability:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:61
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\hat{y} = \\arg\\max_k \\, p(y=k|x)"
msgstr "\\hat{y} = \\arg\\max_k \\, p(y=k|x)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:63
msgid "决策边界是两个类别概率相等的位置：$p(y=i|x) = p(y=j|x)$。"
msgstr "The decision boundary lies where two class probabilities are equal: $p(y=i|x) = p(y=j|x)$."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:65
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{ref}`activation-"
"functions`中讨论的非线性激活函数，正是为了让神经网络能够学习**非线性的决策边界**。没有非线性激活，无论多少层网络都只能学习线性边界。"
msgstr ""
"The non-linear activation functions discussed in {ref}`activation-functions` exist precisely to enable neural networks to learn **non-linear decision boundaries**. Without non-linear activations, no matter how many layers a network has, it can only learn linear boundaries."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:69
msgid "回归任务：发现数值映射的规律"
msgstr "Regression Tasks: Discovering Numerical Mapping Patterns"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:71
msgid "想象你在做物理实验：测量不同拉力下弹簧的伸长量。你发现\"拉力越大，弹簧伸得越长\"。这不是分类问题，因为你不是把拉力分成\"大\"或\"小\"两类，而是要找出**具体的数值关系**。"
msgstr "Imagine conducting a physics experiment measuring spring extension under different pulling forces. You observe that \"the greater the force, the longer the extension.\" This is not a classification problem—you are not sorting force into \"large\" or \"small\" categories, but finding a **precise numerical relationship**."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:73
msgid "**回归的本质**：学习一个**函数映射**，输入一个数值，输出另一个数值。"
msgstr "**Essence of Regression**: Learning a **functional mapping** that takes numerical inputs and produces numerical outputs."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:75
msgid "最简单的回归是**线性回归**：假设输入和输出之间是直线关系。类比：你收集了若干房屋的面积和价格数据，在纸上画散点图，然后画一条最\"拟合\"这些点的直线。"
msgstr "The simplest form of regression is **linear regression**, assuming a straight-line relationship between input and output. By analogy: you collect data on house floor areas and prices, scatter-plot them on paper, and draw the line that best \"fits\" the points."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:77
msgid "**数学形式**：对于单变量线性回归"
msgstr "**Mathematical Formulation**: For single-variable linear regression:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:79
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\hat{y} = wx + b"
msgstr "\\hat{y} = wx + b"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:81
msgid "$x$：输入特征（如房屋面积）"
msgstr "$x$: Input feature (e.g., house floor area)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:82
msgid "$w$：权重（斜率，表示\"每平方米值多少钱\"）"
msgstr "$w$: Weight (slope, representing \"price per square meter\")"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:83
msgid "$b$：偏置（截距，表示\"基础价格\"）"
msgstr "$b$: Bias (intercept, representing \"base price\")"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:84
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$\\hat{y}$：预测值（预测房价）"
msgstr "$\\hat{y}$: Predicted value (predicted house price)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:86
msgid "**几何意义**"
msgstr "**Geometric Interpretation**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:88
msgid "在二维平面上，线性回归就是找一条直线，让所有数据点到直线的**垂直距离之和最小**。"
msgstr "In a 2D plane, linear regression finds a straight line that **minimizes the sum of vertical distances** from all data points to the line."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:91
msgid "线性回归的几何意义"
msgstr "Geometric Meaning of Linear Regression"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:112
msgid "**扩展到多元**：现实中的房价不只由面积决定，还取决于位置、房龄、楼层等。多元线性回归："
msgstr "**Extension to Multiple Variables**: Real-world house prices depend not only on floor area, but also on location, age, floor, etc. Multivariable linear regression:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:114
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\hat{y} = w_1x_1 + w_2x_2 + ... + w_dx_d + b = \\mathbf{w}^T\\mathbf{x} "
"+ b"
msgstr ""
"\\hat{y} = w_1x_1 + w_2x_2 + ... + w_dx_d + b = \\mathbf{w}^T\\mathbf{x} "
"+ b"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:116
msgid "这不再是二维平面上的直线，而是**高维空间中的超平面**。"
msgstr "This is no longer a straight line in a 2D plane, but a **hyperplane in high-dimensional space**."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:118
msgid "**非线性回归**"
msgstr "**Non-linear Regression**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:120
msgid "线性回归假设关系是直线，但很多规律是曲线。神经网络通过堆叠非线性层，可以学习**任意复杂的函数映射**。"
msgstr "Linear regression assumes a straight-line relationship, but many patterns in nature are curved. By stacking non-linear layers, neural networks can learn **arbitrarily complex function mappings**."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:123
msgid "从线性到非线性回归"
msgstr "From Linear to Non-linear Regression"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:146
msgid "回归 vs 分类的本质区别"
msgstr "Fundamental Differences: Regression vs Classification"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:122
msgid "维度"
msgstr "Dimension"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:122
msgid "分类"
msgstr "Classification"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:122
msgid "回归"
msgstr "Regression"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:122
msgid "**规律形式**"
msgstr "**Pattern Form**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:122
msgid "类别边界（划分区域）"
msgstr "Category boundaries (partitioning regions)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:122
msgid "函数映射（输入→输出）"
msgstr "Function mapping (input → output)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:122
msgid "**输出空间**"
msgstr "**Output Space**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:122
#, python-brace-format
msgid "离散有限集 $\\{1,...,K\\}$"
msgstr "Discrete finite set $\\{1,...,K\\}$"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:122
#, python-brace-format
msgid "连续无穷集 $\\mathbb{R}$"
msgstr "Continuous infinite set $\\mathbb{R}$"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:122
msgid "**预测内容**"
msgstr "**Prediction Target**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:122
msgid "\"这是哪一类\""
msgstr "\"Which category is this?\""

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:122
msgid "\"数值是多少\""
msgstr "\"What is the numerical value?\""

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:122
msgid "**误差度量**"
msgstr "**Error Metric**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:122
msgid "分类错误率"
msgstr "Classification error rate"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:122
#, python-brace-format
msgid "数值偏差 $|y - \\hat{y}|$"
msgstr "Numerical deviation $|y - \\hat{y}|$"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:122
msgid "**几何形象**"
msgstr "**Geometric Analogy**"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:122
msgid "空间中的分界曲面"
msgstr "Separating surface in space"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:122
msgid "空间中的拟合曲面"
msgstr "Fitted surface in space"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:156
msgid "**一句话总结**：分类是\"切蛋糕\"（划分空间），回归是\"画曲线\"（拟合关系）。"
msgstr "**Summary in One Sentence**: Classification is \"slicing a cake\" (partitioning space), while regression is \"drawing a curve\" (fitting relationships)."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:160
msgid "自回归任务：发现序列依赖的规律"
msgstr "Autoregressive Tasks: Discovering Sequence Dependency Patterns"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:162
msgid "想象你在听故事：\"从前有座山，山里有座...\"你自然会接\"庙\"。为什么不是\"城堡\"或\"学校\"？因为你学过，\"山里有座\"后面最常接的是\"庙\"。"
msgstr "Imagine listening to a story: \"Once upon a time, there was a mountain, and in the mountain there was a...\" You naturally expect \"temple\". Why not \"castle\" or \"school\"? Because from experience, \"temple\" is the most common word following that context."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:164
msgid "**自回归的本质**：基于**已生成的内容**预测**下一个内容**，一步一步\"续写\"。"
msgstr "**Essence of Autoregression**: Predicting the **next token** based on **already generated content**, step by step."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:166
msgid ""
"**概率分解**：序列的联合概率可以用链式法则分解。对于两个事件，$p(A,B) = p(A) \\cdot "
"p(B|A)$——先发生A，再在A发生的条件下发生B。扩展到序列："
msgstr ""
"**Probability Factorization**: The joint probability of a sequence can be factorized using the chain rule. For two events, $p(A,B) = p(A) \\cdot p(B|A)$—first $A$ occurs, then $B$ occurs given $A$. Extending this to sequences:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:168
msgid "p(y_1, y_2, y_3) = p(y_1) \\cdot p(y_2|y_1) \\cdot p(y_3|y_1, y_2)"
msgstr "p(y_1, y_2, y_3) = p(y_1) \\cdot p(y_2|y_1) \\cdot p(y_3|y_1, y_2)"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:170
msgid "一般形式："
msgstr "General form:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:172
#, python-brace-format
msgid "p(y_1, y_2, ..., y_T) = \\prod_{t=1}^{T} p(y_t | y_{<t})"
msgstr "p(y_1, y_2, ..., y_T) = \\prod_{t=1}^{T} p(y_t | y_{<t})"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:174
#, python-brace-format
msgid "其中 $y_{<t}$ 表示 $y_1$ 到 $y_{t-1}$ 的所有历史内容。"
msgstr "where $y_{<t}$ denotes all historical content from $y_1$ to $y_{t-1}$."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:176
msgid "**为什么这样分解有用？** 想象你要生成句子\"猫坐在垫子上\"。直接学习整个句子的概率很难，但分解后每步都是简单的分类："
msgstr "**Why is this factorization useful?** Imagine generating the sentence \"The cat sat on the mat\". Learning the probability of the entire sentence at once is difficult, but after factorization, every step becomes a simple classification task:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:178
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$p(\\text{猫}|\\text{<s>})$：句首是\"猫\"的概率"
msgstr "$p(\\text{The}|\\text{<s>})$: Probability of starting with \"The\""

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:179
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$p(\\text{坐}|\\text{<s>猫})$：看到\"猫\"后接\"坐\"的概率"
msgstr "$p(\\text{cat}|\\text{<s>The})$: Probability of following \"The\" with \"cat\""

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:180
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$p(\\text{在}|\\text{<s>猫坐})$：看到\"猫坐\"后接\"在\"的概率"
msgstr "$p(\\text{sat}|\\text{<s>The cat})$: Probability of following \"The cat\" with \"sat\""

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:182
msgid "**因果性约束**：自回归只能依赖**过去**，不能\"偷看\"未来："
msgstr "**Causality Constraint**: Autoregression can only depend on the **past**, with no \"peeking\" into the future:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:184
msgid "p(y_t | y_1, ..., y_{t-1}, \\underbrace{y_{t+1}, ...}_{\\text{不能用}})"
msgstr "p(y_t | y_1, ..., y_{t-1}, \\underbrace{y_{t+1}, ...}_{\\text{Cannot use}})"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:186
msgid "这就像写作文——你不能用还没写的句子来决定现在写什么。这种\"只看左边\"的特性称为**因果掩码**。"
msgstr "This is like writing an essay—you cannot use unwritten sentences to decide what to write now. This \"left-only\" property is called **causal masking**."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:188
msgid "**训练 vs 推理**："
msgstr "**Training vs. Inference**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:190
msgid "**训练时**：已知完整序列\"猫坐在垫子上\"，模型同时学习每个位置的条件概率。可以并行计算所有位置的损失。"
msgstr "**During Training**: The full sequence \"The cat sat on the mat\" is known, and the model learns conditional probabilities at all positions simultaneously. Losses across all positions can be computed in parallel."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:191
msgid "**推理时**：从`<start>`开始，生成第一个词，然后用这个词作为输入生成第二个词，依此类推。必须**串行**进行。"
msgstr "**During Inference**: Starting from `<start>`, the model generates the first word, uses it as input to generate the second word, and so on. This must proceed **sequentially**."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:193
msgid "**序列生成的树状结构**："
msgstr "**Tree Structure of Sequence Generation**:"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:196
msgid "自回归的序列生成"
msgstr "Sequence Generation in Autoregression"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:238
msgid "在每一步，模型输出一个概率分布，然后采样（或选择最大概率）得到下一个词。"
msgstr "At each step, the model outputs a probability distribution, then samples (or selects the maximum probability token) to produce the next word."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:240
msgid ""
"**与分类的联系**：自回归的每一步本质上都是分类——从词汇表中选择一个词。区别在于：普通分类的每次预测独立进行；而自回归的每次预测**依赖所有历史选择**，是"
" \"**有记忆的分类**\"。评估时也不只看单步准确率，而是看整个序列的质量（用困惑度衡量）。"
msgstr ""
"**Connection to Classification**: Every step of autoregression is fundamentally classification—selecting a token from a vocabulary. The difference is that standard classification predictions are independent, whereas each autoregressive prediction **depends on all historical choices**—it is \"**classification with memory**\". Evaluation also considers overall sequence quality (measured by perplexity) rather than just single-step accuracy."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:244
msgid "三种任务的统一与差异"
msgstr "Unification and Differences Among the Three Tasks"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:246
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"三类任务都遵循相同的计算框架（见{ref}`computational-graph`）：输入 → 变换 → 输出 → "
"损失计算。差异在于**输出层的设计**和**损失函数的选择**。"
msgstr ""
"All three task types follow the same computational framework (see {ref}`computational-graph`): Input → Transformation → Output → Loss Computation. The key differences lie in **output layer design** and **choice of loss function**."

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:195
msgid "任务"
msgstr "Task"

#: ../../../source/math-fundamentals/task-formulations.md:195
msgid "规律形式"
msgstr "Pattern Form"

